open scoped TensorProduct in
/-- **Upgrade from identified to unconditional weak universality**
(PROVEN — the glue of the Mazur pillar's 2026-07-24 decomposition):
a package that factors residually identified deformations factors ALL
deformations, when `ρbar` is irreducible and hardly ramified.  Given a
test deformation `D`, its reduction `D.ρ.baseChange k` along the
(automatically continuous, `continuous_pi`) reduction map is a
2-dimensional representation over `k` whose `charFrob` at each prime
off `D.S` MATCHES that of `ρbar` in full: the linear coefficients
match by `charFrob_compat` and `charFrob_baseChange`, the constant
coefficients match at EVERY place because both determinants are pinned
to the same cyclotomic value
(`coeff_zero_charFrob_eq_of_isHardlyRamified`, which also consumes the
rigidity `ringHom_padicInt_eq` of `ℤ_p →+* k`), and both polynomials are
monic quadratics (`charFrob_monic`, `charFrob_natDegree`,
`monic_natDegree_two_ext`).  The Chebotarev–Brauer–Nesbitt leaf
`exists_conj_of_charFrob_eq_away` turns the matching into a residual
identification, and the identified factorization applies. -/
theorem isWeaklyUniversal_of_isWeaklyUniversalOnIdentified.{s, t, uK, uW, uR}
    {p : ℕ} {hpodd : Odd p} [Fact p.Prime]
    {k : Type uK} [Field k] [Finite k] [Algebra ℤ_[p] k]
    [TopologicalSpace k] [DiscreteTopology k] [IsTopologicalRing k]
    {W : Type uW} [AddCommGroup W] [Module k W] [Module.Finite k W]
    [Module.Free k W]
    {hW : Module.rank k W = 2} {ρbar : GaloisRep ℚ k W}
    (hρbar : IsHardlyRamified hpodd hW ρbar)
    (hirr : ρbar.IsIrreducible)
    {Runiv : Type uR} [CommRing Runiv] [TopologicalSpace Runiv]
    [IsTopologicalRing Runiv] [IsLocalRing Runiv] [Algebra ℤ_[p] Runiv]
    {ρuniv : GaloisRep ℚ Runiv (Fin 2 → Runiv)} {πuniv : Runiv →+* k}
    (h : IsWeaklyUniversalOnIdentifiedDeformation.{s, t, uK, uW, uR} hpodd
      ρbar ρuniv πuniv) :
    IsWeaklyUniversalDeformation.{s, t, uK, uW, uR} hpodd ρbar ρuniv
      πuniv := by
  intro D
  letI := D.commRing
  letI := D.topologicalSpace
  letI := D.isTopologicalRing
  letI := D.isLocalRing
  letI := D.algebra
  letI := D.addCommGroup
  letI := D.module
  letI := D.moduleFiniteVd
  letI := D.moduleFreeVd
  letI : Algebra D.A k := D.π.toAlgebra
  letI : ContinuousSMul D.A k := continuousSMul_of_algebraMap D.A k
    (by rw [RingHom.algebraMap_toAlgebra]; exact D.continuous_pi)
  refine h D ?_
  -- the reduction is 2-dimensional …
  have hrankW' : Module.rank k (k ⊗[D.A] D.Vd) = 2 := by
    rw [Module.rank_baseChange, D.rank_eq]
    simp
  -- … and its Frobenius characteristic polynomials are those of `ρbar`
  have hcf : ∀ (q : ℕ) (hq : q.Prime),
      hq.toHeightOneSpectrumRingOfIntegersRat ∉ D.S →
      (D.ρ.baseChange k).charFrob hq.toHeightOneSpectrumRingOfIntegersRat =
        ρbar.charFrob hq.toHeightOneSpectrumRingOfIntegersRat := by
    intro q hq hqS
    have hmap := charFrob_baseChange (B := k)
      hq.toHeightOneSpectrumRingOfIntegersRat D.ρ
    rw [RingHom.algebraMap_toAlgebra] at hmap
    refine monic_natDegree_two_ext ?_
      (charFrob_monic hq.toHeightOneSpectrumRingOfIntegersRat ρbar) ?_
      (charFrob_natDegree hq.toHeightOneSpectrumRingOfIntegersRat ρbar hW)
      ?_ ?_
    · rw [hmap]
      exact (charFrob_monic hq.toHeightOneSpectrumRingOfIntegersRat D.ρ).map
        D.π
    · rw [hmap, (charFrob_monic hq.toHeightOneSpectrumRingOfIntegersRat
        D.ρ).natDegree_map D.π]
      exact charFrob_natDegree hq.toHeightOneSpectrumRingOfIntegersRat D.ρ
        D.rank_eq
    · rw [hmap, Polynomial.coeff_map]
      exact coeff_zero_charFrob_eq_of_isHardlyRamified D.isHardlyRamified
        hρbar D.π
        (ringHom_padicInt_eq (D.π.comp (algebraMap ℤ_[p] D.A))
          (algebraMap ℤ_[p] k))
        hq.toHeightOneSpectrumRingOfIntegersRat
    · rw [hmap, Polynomial.coeff_map]
      exact D.charFrob_compat q hq hqS
  obtain ⟨e, he⟩ := exists_conj_of_charFrob_eq_away hW hirr hrankW'
    (D.ρ.baseChange k) D.S hcf
  exact ⟨e, he⟩

set_option linter.checkUnivs false in
/-- **Carayol: a weakly universal deformation may be taken TRACE-GENERATED**
(sorry node, cut 2026-07-29 as the faithfulness repair of
`exists_auxDeformationDiamondControl` far below): from ANY weakly universal
package `(R₀, ρ₀, π₀)` one may pass to a weakly universal package that is
additionally topologically generated over `ℤ_[p]` by its Frobenius traces away
from the exceptional set.

# WHY THIS LEAF EXISTS, AND WHY IT IS THE `∃`-FORM AND NOT AN IMPLICATION

`IsWeaklyUniversalDeformation` is existence-only, and existence-only
universality pins the ring in NO direction: `R₀[[y_1, …, y_m]]` classifies
everything `R₀` does (a classifying map out of `R₀` precomposed with
`MvPowerSeries.constantCoeff` is a classifying map out of the bigger ring).
So the IMPLICATION "weakly universal ⟹ trace-generated" is **FALSE**, with
that family as the witness, and stating this leaf that way would manufacture a
false node.  What is true — and what Carayol's theorem gives — is that one may
DESCEND: the closed `ℤ_[p]`-subalgebra generated by the traces carries `ρ₀`
(absolute irreducibility of `ρbar` is exactly the hypothesis for that descent),
it inherits weak universality because classifying maps restrict along it, and
it is trace-generated by construction.  Hence the existential form.

**This is not decoration; it is what makes `R = 𝕋` true.**
`injective_ringHom_of_isWeaklyUniversal` below is FALSE without it: for
`Runiv = R₀[[y]]`, still weakly universal, the classifying map
`ψ : Runiv →+* T` may send `y ↦ 0` while satisfying every trace and
`ℤ_[p]`-structure clause, so `ψ` is not injective.  The same inflation refutes
`exists_auxDeformationDiamondControl`'s control map far below (see its FALSITY
AUDIT).  Both are repaired by the single clause this leaf supplies.

References: Carayol, in *p-adic monodromy and the Birch–Swinnerton-Dyer
conjecture*, Contemp. Math. 165 (1994), Thm. 3 (deformations descend to the
trace subring for absolutely irreducible residual representations); Mazur, in
*Galois Groups over ℚ* (1989), §1.4 and §1.9; Nyssen, Manuscripta Math. 89
(1996); Rouquier, J. Algebra 180 (1996).

CIRCULARITY GUARD: as for `exists_weaklyUniversal_hardlyRamifiedDeformation`
below — a proof discharging this by `exfalso` from the odd-prime dichotomy
against `hirr` and `hρbar` must be rejected.

# CONDITIONAL FALSITY AUDIT (2026-07-30) — THIS LEAF HAS NO NON-CIRCULAR PROOF

Read this BEFORE attacking the leaf.  It is not refuted — the hypothesis set is
classically empty, so it is true outright, exactly like its neighbours — but the
statement forces a consequence that is FALSE in the non-vacuous world, so **every
proof of it must pass through the odd-prime dichotomy the guard above bans.**
Attacking it as stated is wasted work; it wants a restatement first, and the
restatement is a design decision for the owner of `IsTraceGeneratedDeformation`,
not something a prover agent should make unilaterally.

*The forced consequence.*  Suppose the conclusion holds, with witnesses `Runiv`,
`ρuniv`, `πuniv`, `Suniv`.  Then

* `πuniv` is automatically the RESIDUE MAP and automatically CONTINUOUS.  It is
  surjective onto the field `k`, so `ker πuniv` is a maximal ideal of `Runiv`;
  `Runiv` is local, so `ker πuniv = 𝔪`; and `IsAdic (maximalIdeal Runiv)` makes
  `𝔪` open, so every fibre of `πuniv` is a coset of an open subgroup.
* `πuniv` is a `ℤ_[p]`-algebra map, by the rigidity `ringHom_padicInt_eq` that
  `isWeaklyUniversal_of_isWeaklyUniversalOnIdentified` above already uses.
* Hence `πuniv (Algebra.adjoin ℤ_[p] S) = Algebra.adjoin ℤ_[p] (πuniv '' S)`,
  and since `k` is DISCRETE every subset of it is closed, so
  `πuniv (A.topologicalClosure) ⊆ πuniv A`.
* With `S` the trace set of `ρuniv` away from `Suniv`, `hunivred` says
  `πuniv '' S = {(ρbar.charFrob q).coeff 1 | q ∉ Suniv}`.

Chaining these with `IsTraceGeneratedDeformation p ρuniv Suniv` and surjectivity
of `πuniv` gives

>  `k = Algebra.adjoin ℤ_[p] {(ρbar.charFrob q).coeff 1 | q prime, q ∉ Suniv}`,

i.e. **`k` is generated over `𝔽_p` by the Frobenius traces of `ρbar` away from a
finite set.**  Nothing in the hypotheses says that, and it is false in general.

*The witness, and it is a completely ordinary one.*  Let `ρbar₀` be hardly
ramified and absolutely irreducible over `k₀`, and set `k = k₀(α)` a proper
finite extension, `W = k ⊗_{k₀} W₀`, `ρbar = ρbar₀ ⊗ k`.  Every hypothesis
survives verbatim: `IsHardlyRamified`'s four fields (`det`, `isUnramified`,
`isFlat`, `isTameAtTwo` — see `HardlyRamified/Defs.lean`) are all stable under
extension of the coefficient field, `Module.rank k W = 2` is stable, `Finite k`
is stable, and `ρbar.IsIrreducible` holds because `ρbar₀` was ABSOLUTELY
irreducible.  A weakly universal package over `k` exists classically (Mazur's
theory is insensitive to the coefficient field).  But every `charFrob`
coefficient of `ρbar` lies in `k₀`, so the displayed subalgebra is contained in
`k₀ ⊊ k` — for EVERY finite `Suniv`, no Chebotarev input needed.  The conclusion
is unreachable.

So the leaf is true only because no `(hpodd, hρbar, hirr)` exists at all, and any
proof must exhibit that.  That is the banned discharge.

*What repairs it.*  The defect is in `IsTraceGeneratedDeformation`, which adjoins
over `ℤ_[p]` where Carayol adjoins over a COEFFICIENT RING for `k`.  Carayol's
theorem is "`Runiv` is topologically generated by traces over `𝕎 k`", and `𝕎 k`
surjects onto `k` while `ℤ_[p]` does not.  Two shapes, both expressible today:

1. *Cohen-base.*  Adjoin over the image of the Cohen coefficient map instead of
   over `ℤ_[p]`.  This module already has that map — `IsCohenCoefficients` and
   `exists_ringHom_wittVector_of_isAdicComplete`, both above — so the repair
   costs no new theory.  It adds an argument, hence changes the predicate's
   ARITY at every use.
2. *Arity-preserving.*  Replace the equation by: every CLOSED `ℤ_[p]`-subalgebra
   that contains the traces and surjects onto the residue field is `⊤`.  This is
   strictly weaker than the present clause, still kills the `R₀[[y]]` inflation
   (there the image of `R₀` is closed, contains every trace, surjects onto the
   residue field, and is not `⊤`), and is what Carayol gives once one knows a
   closed subring of a complete local ring surjecting onto the residue field
   contains a coefficient ring.

*Blast radius, measured.*  `IsTraceGeneratedDeformation` occurs ONLY in this
module (checked by `grep -rn` over `Fermat/`), at nine `(hgen : …)` binders, and
**every one of them merely THREADS `hgen` onward — no proof in the tree consumes
its strength today.**  So either repair is mechanical right now and will stop
being mechanical as soon as the first consumer is written.  That is the argument
for doing it soon, and the reason this audit is recorded rather than acted on
here: it changes an interface across ten signatures, which is the split this
module lost two release build rounds to on 2026-07-30. -/
theorem exists_traceGenerated_of_isWeaklyUniversal.{t, uK, uW, uR}
    {p : ℕ} (hpodd : Odd p) [Fact p.Prime]
    {k : Type uK} [Field k] [Finite k] [Algebra ℤ_[p] k]
    [TopologicalSpace k] [DiscreteTopology k] [IsTopologicalRing k]
    {W : Type uW} [AddCommGroup W] [Module k W] [Module.Finite k W]
    [Module.Free k W]
    (hW : Module.rank k W = 2) {ρbar : GaloisRep ℚ k W}
    (hρbar : IsHardlyRamified hpodd hW ρbar)
    (hirr : ρbar.IsIrreducible)
    {R₀ : Type uR} [CommRing R₀] [TopologicalSpace R₀] [IsTopologicalRing R₀]
