# HOW IT IS PROVEN, AND WHY IT IS CHEAPER THAN THE ROUTE FIRST RECORDED

The route recorded when this leaf was cut went through the procyclic
identification `H¹(G_q/I_q, M) ≅ M/(ρ Frob_q - 1)M`, using `hcunr` to see
the restriction of `c` at `q` as INFLATED from `G_q/I_q`.  That is the
right picture for the `↔`, and it is **not needed for the implication
actually asserted here**, which is the easy direction only.

The proof is instead this.  `c ∈ ker (locResDecompTwist1 … q)` says the
class of `z` dies under `ContinuousCohomology.map (decompHom q) (𝟙 _) 1`.
By `ContinuousCohomology.cocycleClass_eq_zero_iff` on the `G_q`-side, the
RESTRICTED cocycle `cochainsMap (decompHom q) (𝟙 _) z` is then a
COBOUNDARY `d y`; and a coboundary has

    eval₁ (d y) σ  =  y σ − y 1  =  ρ σ (y 1) − y 1

for EVERY `σ`, by degree-`0` homogeneity of `y` — one witness `y 1` serving
all `σ` at once.  Taking `σ = Frob_q ∈ G_q` and pushing forward along
`decompHom q` gives `z (globalFrob q) ∈ (ρ (globalFrob q) − 1) · M`, i.e.
`globalFrob q ∉ survivingLocus`, contradicting `hmem`.

So vanishing of the restriction to the WHOLE decomposition group already
produces the boundary witness on the nose; nothing has to be inflated back
from the quotient, and consequently **neither `hcunr` nor `q ∉ {2, p}` is
used** — they are kept in the signature (underscored) because the consumer
`exists_separatingOpen_locResDecomp` holds them anyway and because they are
part of the statement of DDT 2.48 as cited.  The leaf is therefore proven
in a strictly stronger form than stated.  It is emphatically NOT vacuous:
`hmem` is the whole content, and it is discharged by an explicit witness
extracted from the vanishing hypothesis.

The general machinery lives in
`Fermat/FLT/Mathlib/RepresentationTheory/Homological/ContCohomology/LowDegreeOne.lean`,
which acquired three lemmas for this: `homogeneousCochains_zero_apply_smul`
and `eval₁_mem_range_sub_of_mem_range_bdryKer` (the coboundary computation),
`cocycleClass_eq_homologyπ` (identifying the concrete `cocycleClass` of
`ContCohomology/Basic.lean` with the categorical `homologyπ`, which is what
makes `cocycleClass` compatible with `ContinuousCohomology.map`), and
`eval₁_mem_range_sub_of_map_cocycleClass_eq_zero` assembling them.

`globalFrob q = decompHom q (adicArithFrob q)` holds only up to the choice
of the ring map `ℚ →+* ℚ_q` inside each; the two are identified by
`Subsingleton.elim` on `ℚ →+* ℚ_q`, exactly as `MazurTorsion.lean` does.

Note that no local Tate duality is needed, in keeping with the deviation
note on `IsTaylorWilesPrimeSet`.

