# WHAT WAS **NOT** DONE, AND WHY: THE LEVEL CLAUSE STAYS AN INCLUSION

A repair proposed elsewhere is to strengthen clause 3 from
`taylorWilesLevelIdeal p (fun _ => n) ≤ RingHom.ker diamond` to an EQUALITY, on
the ground that the inclusion admits the junk `diamond` killing every `S_i`.
That is declined here, on two independent grounds, each checkable:

1. **The junk diamond is ALREADY excluded on this leaf, and on the consumers
   that matter.**  It is excluded here by the pairing
   `ker toRuniv = (taylorWilesAug p q).map diamond` — the both-directions
   vacuity check at the head of this docstring is precisely that argument.  It
   is excluded in the `ℚ`-side Hecke leaf because
   `exists_auxHeckeCoordModuleData` below carries that same `hker` alongside
   its `hbn`.  And the Hilbert twin does too: `exists_hilbertAuxHeckeModuleData`
   (`HilbertModularity.lean`) carries
   `hker : RingHom.ker toRuniv = (Modularity.taylorWilesAug ℓ q).map diamond`
   in the binder immediately above `hbex`.  So the claim that `hbex` alone
   admits the degenerate `diamond` overlooks `hker`; with `hker` present the
   degenerate map forces `toRuniv` injective, which is a vacuous hypothesis
   package rather than a false conclusion.
2. **The equality would make THIS leaf false whenever `v_p(q_i − 1) > n`, which
   `hQ` forces.**  `hQ` is asked at level `n + 1`, so each `q_i ≡ 1 mod p^{n+1}`
   and the tame quotient `Δ_{q_i}` has order `p^{e_i}` with `e_i ≥ n + 1`.
   Write `σ_i ∈ 𝒟Q.R^×` for the image of a generator of `Δ_{q_i}`.  Clause 2
   pins `(diamond S_1, …, diamond S_q) = ker toRuniv = (σ_1 − 1, …, σ_q − 1)`,
   the augmentation ideal.  An EQUALITY in clause 3 pins `1 + diamond S_i` to be
   a unit of order exactly `p^n`, hence (in `ℤ_p[Δ_{q_i}]`, where the
   `p^n`-torsion units are the group-like `σ_i^{p^{e_i − n}}`) forces
   `diamond S_i = σ_i^{p^{e_i-n}} − 1` up to the ideal it generates — and
   `ℤ_p[ℤ/p^{e}] ⧸ (σ^{p^{m}} − 1) ≅ ℤ_p[ℤ/p^{m}] ≠ ℤ_p = ℤ_p[ℤ/p^e] ⧸ (σ − 1)`
   for `m ≥ 1`, so the two ideals differ and clauses 2 and 3 become jointly
   unsatisfiable.  The witness is that group-ring computation; it needs no model
   of the deformation problem beyond `ℤ_p[Δ_Q] ↪ 𝒟Q.R`.

   The SAFE strengthening, if one is wanted, is therefore the exponent-vector
   form `∃ e : Fin q → ℕ, (∀ i, n ≤ e i) ∧ RingHom.ker diamond =
   taylorWilesLevelIdeal p e`, which is what `TaylorWilesLevelRaw.bIdeal` is
   shaped for and what `exists_taylorWilesAuxLevelData` below already produces
   (it currently hard-codes `e ≡ n`).  Making that change means revisiting the
   constant-exponent choice and the coordinate model in the assembly and both
   Hecke leaves — a cut-level change across owners, flagged here rather than
   made.  It is also the place to re-examine the EXPONENT AUDIT of
   `exists_taylorWilesAuxLevelPresentedDatum`, which asserts the constant vector
   is "the standard formulation and not a weakening": the computation above says
   the constant vector is only admissible when `e_i = n`, and
   `IsRaisedLevelHardlyRamified.isSplitTorusAt` puts NO order bound on the
   inertia character `χ`, so nothing in the deformation problem caps it at
