# — THE SURJECTIVITY OF THE CONTROL MAP IS NO LONGER A LEAF

The three-item list above says what remains, and item 1 — `toRuniv` is
SURJECTIVE — is now discharged here rather than owed.  What this theorem does:

1. **Build the control map.**  `exists_auxDeformationDatum` above now NAMES its
   carrier, so it yields a level-`Q` datum `𝒟` together with
   `ee : 𝒟.R ≃+* Runiv` and the three compatibilities (`ℤ_[p]`-algebra, `πuniv`,
   and `charFrob` at EVERY place).  `hQ` is asked at level `n + 1`, which is
   `≥ 1`, so that leaf's `hn` is discharged by `Nat.succ_le_succ`.  Feeding `𝒟`
   to `h𝒟Q` gives the classifying map `f : 𝒟Q.R →+* 𝒟.R`, and
   `toRuniv₀ := ee ∘ f` inherits all three compatibilities — the `charFrob` one
   through `Polynomial.coeff_map` applied to `𝒟`'s clause.  **This is where the
   removed provability obstruction is cashed in**, and it is the only consumer of
   that strengthening in the file.
2. **Hand it to the sub-leaf**, which returns the exponent vector, the diamonds,
   a control map (not necessarily `toRuniv₀`) and the two kernel clauses,
   together with the same three compatibilities.
3. **Prove the returned map surjective** by `surjective_of_isTraceGeneratedDeformation`
   above: `𝒟Q.R` is compact (Noetherian, local, maximal-adically complete,
   `Finite` residue field), so the range is closed in the Hausdorff `Runiv`, and
   it contains the traces off the sub-leaf's finite set, whose closed
   `ℤ_[p]`-span is `⊤` by `hgen` and `isTraceGeneratedDeformation_exchange`.
   That exchange lemma is what removes the "finitely many remaining places are
   the residual work" caveat of item 1: `hgen`'s exceptional set and the
   classifying map's exceptional set are unrelated, and by Chebotarev density
   neither restricts the closed span.

So what is left of this leaf is items 2 and 3 only — the control kernel identity
and the diamonds — and they live in
`exists_auxDeformationDiamondControlCompat`.  **The decomposition creates NO new
obligation**: `compactSpace_of_isAdicComplete_of_finite_residueField`, the one
statement it needed that did not exist, is PROVEN (twenty lines, over mathlib's
`IsAdic.isPrecomplete_iff` bridge), so the sorry count is unchanged and one whole
